{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:08f15d2229d4a0c0","name":"Blackguard Minion","source":{"id":"source:reference-08f15d2229d4a0c0","title":"Blackguard Minion","revision":16253,"timestamp":"2024-08-18T00:56:34Z","sha256":"9c8eb3275bdc11f66fd26a6b3072d40ea351b6cfc258f01f7a8d6b40f4f85c08","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=16253","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=Blackguard%20Minion&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-08f15d2229d4a0c0","blocks":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Jedi Academy Training Manual"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Jedi_Academy_Training_Manual"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Affiliations: ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Blackguard"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Blackguard","referenceId":"reference:e4d5dd88946cc424"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["The Blackguard"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Blackguard","referenceId":"reference:e4d5dd88946cc424"}," is a Dark Side cult that seeks to increase its knowledge and power by searching for secrets held by ",{"tag":"a","children":["Force Traditions"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Force_Traditions","referenceId":"reference:da4e2621bc8ff060"}," all over the galaxy.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Shortly before the Battle of ",{"tag":"a","children":["Ruusan"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Ruusan","referenceId":"reference:68adb98c0737f8de"},", a dark apprentice of Kaan named ",{"tag":"a","children":["Vulta Daanat"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Vulta_Daanat?action=edit&redlink=1"}," comes to the belief that ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Force"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Force","referenceId":"reference:67fe90e919b74d0f"}," not only serves as a source of personal power but also a means to understand the universe. Kaan disagrees, intent on exterminating ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Jedi"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Jedi","referenceId":"reference:d320edb17de6c558"}," and conquering ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Old Republic"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Old_Republic","referenceId":"reference:6517b7e15507b001"},". Their disagreement turns physical, and the subsequent ",{"tag":"a","children":["Lightsaber"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Lightsaber","referenceId":"reference:987a817de9003439"}," duel leaves Daanat badly injured, and Kaan leaves him for dead. Daanat nurses his wounds and escapes from ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Brotherhood of Darkness"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Brotherhood_of_Darkness?action=edit&redlink=1"},". After a time, he searches the galaxy, following rumors and leads to various Force-related artifacts. He learns many secrets about ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Dark Side"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Dark_Side"},", settles within the Southern Jedi Ruins on ",{"tag":"a","children":["Mustafar"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Mustafar","referenceId":"reference:1233775240ba356a"},", and takes on several apprentices to pass his knowledge to a new generation of darksiders.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Over time, the cult fluctuates in size, at times growing to mammoth proportions, and shrinking at other times to a mere handful of apprentices. ",{"tag":"a","children":["San'sii the Kursk"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/San%27sii_the_Kursk?action=edit&redlink=1"},", the most recent leader of ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Blackguard"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Blackguard","referenceId":"reference:e4d5dd88946cc424"},", feels the need for more people under his command to help the cult survive. He adopts the practice of recruiting non-Force-sensitive people into the cult's ranks. Donning black armor and bearing ",{"tag":"a","children":["Blaster Rifles"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Blaster_Rifles"},", these ",{"tag":"a","children":["Blackguard Minions"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Blackguard_Minions?action=edit&redlink=1"}," act as soldiers and become the most visible members of the faction, leading many to believe that ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Blackguard"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Blackguard","referenceId":"reference:e4d5dd88946cc424"}," is a paramilitary organization.\n"]},"\n\n",{"tag":"h3","children":["Blackguard Minion Encounters"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["The Blackguard"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Blackguard","referenceId":"reference:e4d5dd88946cc424"}," is found almost exclusively on ",{"tag":"a","children":["Mustafar"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Mustafar","referenceId":"reference:1233775240ba356a"}," in or near the Southern Jedi Ruins, but a few are occasionally located wandering between the ruins and the planet's only remaining city of Fralideja. ",{"tag":"a","children":["Blackguard Wilders"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Blackguard_Wilders?action=edit&redlink=1"}," exist and act more as squad leaders, giving evidence that ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Blackguard"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Blackguard","referenceId":"reference:e4d5dd88946cc424"}," might be better organized than most people think possible of a Dark Side cult.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h2","children":["Blackguard Minion Statistics (CL 1)"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["Medium ",{"tag":"a","children":["Human"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Human","referenceId":"reference:9ffa865f2bc6e850"}," ",{"tag":"a","children":["Nonheroic"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Nonheroic","referenceId":"reference:1bca2ef1d9ebe1c3"}," 3\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Dark Side Score"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Dark_Side_Score"},":"]}," 4\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Initiative"],"href":"https://sws